# 8. COMPLEXITY CONTROL

The generated prompt must actively prevent overengineering.

Prefer the simplest architecture that satisfies:

* functional requirements
* quality requirements
* security requirements
* scale requirements
* reliability requirements
* operational requirements

Possible architecture forms include:

* modular monolith
* service-oriented architecture
* microservices
* event-driven architecture
* serverless
* hybrid architecture
* distributed architecture

Use microservices only when service boundaries and independent operational/deployment needs justify them.

Use event-driven architecture only where asynchronous decoupling, event propagation, integration, throughput, or workflow characteristics justify it.

Use serverless only where the workload characteristics make the operational and economic model appropriate.

Never create infrastructure merely because the prompt mentioned it.

